<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 1) (Ambystoma mexicanum)",
        "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Ambystoma mexicanum morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ambystoma mexicanum specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Ambystoma mexicanum" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A second independent assessor",
        "does_not_claim: That a perfect cos+cos lattice is the geometry of the larval micrograph",
        "does_not_claim: That the species-gallery limb plate is a pigment specimen",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pixel segmentation of the CC BY-SA chromatophore micrograph",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b, Dv/Du) = (0.10, 0.90, 9) with Du set so onset λ = 184.3 µm",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spectral integration, dispersion sweep, and Dv = Du ablation",
        "reported_in_source: Epperlein & Löfberg 1989 larval Ambystoma mexicanum pigment pattern",
        "reported_in_source: Frost-Mason & Mason 1996 review of axolotl pigmentation",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981 coat pre-pattern and the domain-growth scale argument",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the diffusion-driven instability conditions",
        "transfer_boundary: Adult ocellus size is the same species at a longer scale, not a second chronospecies, and is not fitted",
        "transfer_boundary: No cited axolotl paper measured 184.3 µm; that length is the slot's scale coordinate",
        "transfer_boundary: The micrograph has no scale bar, so pixel fractions are not converted to micrometres" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Ambystoma mexicanum; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the diffusion-driven instability conditions | Murray 1981 coat pre-pattern and the domain-growth scale argument | Epperlein & Löfberg 1989 larval Ambystoma mexicanum pigment pattern | Frost-Mason & Mason 1996 review of axolotl pigmentation; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b, Dv/Du) = (0.10, 0.90, 9) with Du set so onset λ = 184.3 µm | Spectral integration, dispersion sweep, and Dv = Du ablation | Pixel segmentation of the CC BY-SA chromatophore micrograph; transfer_boundary: No cited axolotl paper measured 184.3 µm; that length is the slot's scale coordinate | The micrograph has no scale bar, so pixel fractions are not converted to micrometres | Adult ocellus size is the same species at a longer scale, not a second chronospecies, and is not fitted; does_not_claim: That the species-gallery limb plate is a pigment specimen | That a perfect cos+cos lattice is the geometry of the larval micrograph | A second independent assessor]; phenomenon_size: 174 µm (0.0001742 m, log10=-3.759 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 174 µm to 27.9 cm): 174 µm:ambystoma-maculatum-bioelectric-polarity, 324 µm:ambystoma-maculatum-vertex-packing, 6.2 mm:ambystoma-maculatum-turing-wavelength, 1.1 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-clock-wavefront, 3.7 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-morphogen-condensation, 4.8 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-flux-canalization, 5.1 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-elastic-buckling, 6.3 cm:ambystoma-maculatum-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-75056-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/bf00219740>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0749.1993.tb00611.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.8877441> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
