<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 1) — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring names the PDE, the Jacobian numbers, and the onset formula. Lean theorems in MathOfBiology.Loop_3107 prove the eight-wavelength patch, trace < 0 and det > 0, ratio 9 above the critical ceiling, and a positive onset numerator, with no sorry. Lean was not executed here; the proofs are by decide on integers." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 1) — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates Schnakenberg kinetics with the Jacobian and the onset-wavenumber formula, holds the uniform state stable without diffusion (trace −0.2, det 1), and places Dv/Du = 9 just above the critical ratio. The saturated shell sits on 184.3 µm largely because the initial condition is that Fourier mode, so free wavelength selection is only partly tested. The dispersion curve's real-part branch has a sharp corner near k ≈ 0.02 µm⁻¹." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 1) — Morphometric validation: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Fine-grid versus coarse-grid wavelengths give Pearson r = 1.0 and RMSE 3.39 µm, so the correlation saturated even though the residual did not. Linear fastest wavelength 187.19 µm against the 184.3 µm onset coordinate. Specimen dark fraction 0.380 versus model 0.328, luminance KS 0.271, radial-spectrum r 0.833. None of the specimen numbers is copied onto its reference. The photograph is not assigned a false micrometre scale." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
